<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 760 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 760 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 760 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 98 million stg in bills outright and 662 million in repos to July 29.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 1.266 billion stg on Wednesday in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.25 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
